B.afM=new A.eF("Mustard / Canola","February 15 \u2013 March 5","Aphid Surge & Sudden Temperature Spike","NASA POWER T2M & RH2M","Cloudy, warm weather stimulates aphid proliferation, draining sap from flower stalks.","Deploy yellow sticky traps; apply neem-based biopesticide or systemic foliar control at first pest sighting.")
B.afN=new A.eF("Sunflower","May 15 \u2013 June 10","Desiccating Heat Winds & Moisture Deficit","NASA POWER T2M_MAX & Wind Speed","Hot desiccating winds during pollination can dry pollen grains, causing empty central seeds.","Schedule irrigation at bud opening and flowering stages; ensure border shelterbelts.")
B.afO=new A.eF("Garbanzo","April 15 \u2013 May 20","Early Summer Heat Spike (>36\xb0C)","NASA POWER T2M_MAX","Sudden high temperatures cause flower drop if plants are moisture-stressed.","Ensure light drip irrigation during early pod formation.")
B.afP=new A.eF("Blackeye Cowpea","August 15 \u2013 September 10","Lygus Bug Infiltration & Heat","NASA POWER T2M & Relative Humidity","Lygus bugs puncture developing seeds, causing blemished eye spots.","Deploy sweep net scouting; maintain perimeter alfalfa trap strips.")
B.afQ=new A.eF("Winter Camelina","May 1 \u2013 May 20","Early Heat Blast (>32\xb0C)","NASA POWER T2M_MAX","Premature ripening reducing oil content in seed pods.","Select early-flowering cold-hardy varieties.")
B.afR=new A.eF("Bare Spring Field","April 1 \u2013 May 10","Intense Storm Runoff & Soil Erosion","NASA GPM IMERG & SRTM Elevation","Convective spring deluges dislodge uncovered topsoil, carving rills along drainage contours.","Retain winter cover crop biomass or adopt strip-till residue management.")
B.afS=new A.eF("Bare Summer Soil","May 1 \u2013 June 20","Extreme Thermal & Wind Erosion","NASA MODIS NDVI & SRTM Slope Channels","High solar irradiance oxidizes soil organic carbon; gusty pre-monsoon dust storms blow loose topsoil.","Establish a living green mulch or retain zero-till standing residue stubble.")
B.afT=new A.eF("Brachiaria Stubble","August 1 \u2013 August 31","Accidental Wildfire Risk","NASA MODIS Active Fire & FIRMS","Dry standing grass biomass is vulnerable to escaped roadside brush fires.","Maintain 5-meter clean boundary firebreaks around the parcel perimeter.")
B.afU=new A.eF("Alfalfa Stand","January 15 \u2013 February 28","Extreme Cold Without Snowpack (< -15\xb0C)","NASA POWER T2M_MIN","Sub-zero temperatures without snow insulation damage root crowns (winter-kill).","Leave 6 inches of fall stubble to trap drifting snowpack insulation.")
B.afV=new A.eF("Desmodium Seedlings","March 20 \u2013 April 15","Early Season Moisture Deficit","NASA POWER PRECTOTCORR & SMAP Surface Wetness","Shallow rootlets dry out if early rains pause for >10 days.","Plant into pre-moistened seedbed; apply light mulch cover.")
B.afW=new A.eF("Chickpea","January 10 \u2013 February 15","Cloudiness & High Humidity Disease Spread","NASA POWER ALLSKY_SFC_SW_DWN & T2M","Prolonged fog or overcast skies trigger flower drop and Ascochyta fungal spore development.","Maintain wide row spacing (30 cm) for canopy ventilation; avoid excess vegetative irrigation.")
B.afX=new A.eF("Winter Cereal Rye","April 15 \u2013 May 1","Spring Deluge Delaying Field Entry","NASA POWER PRECTOTCORR & SMAP Wetness","Excessively wet soil delays tractor termination, allowing rye to grow excessively tall and tie up nitrogen.","Plan termination at 12\u201318 inches height; consider roller-crimper on firm soil.")
